  "releaseNotes": "- A query's row reader is compiled once per shape and reused when the query runs again, with any captured values: a run no longer compiles and JITs a new delegate. Unchanged where the runtime interprets lambdas (IsDynamicCodeSupported false)\n- Values a query reads once (a captured variable's member, a sub-query's source, a method call on captured values) are read by reflection, and other one-off expressions are interpreted where the runtime can (not on .NET Framework), instead of compiled\n- An exception thrown while evaluating a query's captured value is raised as it is, not wrapped in TargetInvocationException",
  "summary": "Type providers for Firebird database access.",
